  "verbalization": "The compound [(1R,2R,4S,6S,9R,10S,13S,14S,16R)-2,16-dihydroxy-14-(methoxymethyl)-5,5,9-trimethyl-11,15-dioxo-6-tetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9]hexadecanyl] acetate appears to be a target of multiple pathways leading to SNU-387. It is directly linked to Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta, which in turn is targeted by alpha-D-Mannosamine, and alpha-D-Mannosamine is also a target of another compound, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which also targets SNU-387. Additionally, the compound is linked to MIP, which is targeted by two different compounds that both target SNU-387. These findings suggest that the compound may act as a central node in a complex network of interactions that ultimately lead to the activation of SNU-387. The evidence supports a potential role for this compound in modulating SNU-387 through multiple downstream pathways, highlighting its potential as a key player in the biological response to this compound.",
